  "notes": "The research calls this \"one of the few lanes here that is genuinely full-time\", and that single sentence rewrites more of the parent than anything else in this batch: `halfTime` false, BPM down to 90–96 straight, and `snare.placement` back to `backbeat_24`. The added 3-backbeat accent the research names is authored as a high-probability ghost pinned to beat 3 — it is the one place the trap ancestry still shows. Harmony is pop-rock: major and Mixolydian over I–V–vi–IV and vi–IV–I–V with triads at 0.8, and `session.keys` carries major spellings because the parent's are all minor. ⚠ `bassline.rhythm` is `boom_chick`, the only one in this batch. The research says \"root-fifth motion, minimal glide\" over a kick on 1 and 3, and `boom_chick` is the vocabulary's root-fifth alternation — `mirror_kick` would have produced roots only. The 808 register is an octave above every other entry here because the line is guitar-derived rather than sub-derived. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates this high-medium. ⚠ The strict pop form the research describes (intro / verse / pre-chorus / chorus / verse / chorus / bridge / double chorus) is NOT authored: the arrangement section vocabulary is intro / verse / hook / bridge / outro and has no pre-chorus or double-chorus, so writing it would have been authoring dead names. This is the entry to revisit first if that vocabulary ever grows.",
